  "title": "Latin and the Romance languages",
  "summary": "Latin was the language of ancient Rome through the Republic and the Empire, which in the West lasted until 476 CE. The Romance languages descend from the Latin of the Roman Empire; their name comes from a medieval Latin word for a Latin vernacular. The Church kept Latin in its rituals long after the Empire fell.",
